# Results are TRACKED, deliberately.
#
# Every module under research/ used to write its grids to /tmp, which does not
# survive a container recycle. That is why the V11 stop sweep (459 cells), the
# V21 ADX x CHOP grid (110 cells) and the V24 grid could not be audited: the
# code and the study prose survived, the per-cell numbers did not.
#
# So this directory inverts the usual rule -- ignore everything, then re-admit
# the result formats -- rather than ignoring outputs as build artefacts.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!*.csv
!*.json
!*.txt
!*.md

# Parquet IS admitted: it is how a seven-figure grid becomes storable. V42's 1,131,227-cell
# sweep is 192 MB as CSV -- past GitHub's 100 MB hard limit, and it failed the push with a 408
# before this rule existed -- and 29 MB as zstd parquet with the same rows. This repo already
# tracks parquet grids under research/turtle/.
!*.parquet

# Other binary intermediates stay out: caches and chunk files, not results.
*.npy
*.npz
*.pkl

# the two trend-day sweeps are 512 MB of intermediate cells; the analyses are committed instead
trendday/sweep_*.csv
trendday/dc_*.csv
vwapdrift/grid_*.csv
